WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.510
I restrung it myself.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.950
Tsukimori-kun taught me how.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.870
I'm so glad I met this violin.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:15.320
I can finally turn back to face the things I've been avoiding until now.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.490
Hino, it's all thanks to you, I'm grateful.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.060
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.410
Your playing has changed considerably.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:31.310
But there's another who has changed as well.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.060
A Fanfare for You.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.880
Have you heard Hino's playing?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.960
Yeah, it's awful. Why hasn't she withdrawn?

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:36.210
I guess after coming this far her true colors as a General Studies student show through.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.500
Will she even be able to appear for the final selection at this rate?

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.350
You know, it's like, just give it up already, Hino-san.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.890
Well it doesn't affect us, but the Music Department people are really complaining.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.380
There's been a lot of trouble during this competition, hasn't there?

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.550
Yes, it's mostly the effect of Hino participating.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.580
It really feels like the competition is basically over now, doesn't it?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.660
It was a mistake to have someone from General Studies participate in the first place.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.060
That student from General Studies is obviously going to get last place.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.130
It was impossible for her from the start.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.930
Hihara, is it OK for you not to be practicing?

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.920
You've got to sprint headlong into the final selection, this is your last chance, you know.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.380
Yeah.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:32.940
Yeah.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:38.070
With Yunoki leaving, what are we Music Department third-years going to do if you slack of?

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.950
What is the team supposed to do with you?!

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.200
Don't give up on that grand prize yet!

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.560
Grand prize?

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:53.680
By the way... That's my seat.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:55.960
Ah! S-Sorry!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:02.430
You know you're getting kinda fat.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.930
Kanayan.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:10.990
What? You look like some depressed teenager.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.090
It totally doesn't suit you.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.240
Is it not good enough just to like something?

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.980
I just don't get it.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:23.650
The grand prize, who gets what place...

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.620
Competitions are that kind of thing, you see.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:32.140
But I didn't start playing music to compete with other people.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:37.190
But the person you're competing with isn't the other participants, it's yourself.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.890
Whether you can put it all out there...

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:46.090
Whether you can struggle to improve just a little bit more...

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.900
Whether you can stop making excuses to yourself...

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:52.850
In the end, it's really just a way to surpass who you were yesterday.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.110
Who I was yesterday...

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:04.550
Man, what am I doing say such cliche teacher-like things!

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.240
Don't go thinking about it over and over in your head.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.720
Try thinking it out with your trumpet.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.000
With your own music.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.660
With my music?

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.670
Sheesh, like I should talk.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.960
How nice it must be to be young...

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.480
Worry all you want, young one.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.800
Hihara-sempai?

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.220
He sounds different than before somehow.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.180
But there's another who has changed as well.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.330
He was talking about Hihara-sempai.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.520
Kaho-chan.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.850
Hihara-sempai, um...

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:57.310
I've been thinking a lot about why I decided to play the trumpet, you see.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.690
I might have mentioned it before, but I was in track and field until first year of middle school.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:08.650
I had a really great friend ever since elementary school. We were always together.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.290
A new personal best!

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.750
Oh, really?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.390
You did it, Kazuki!

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:24.530
And you improved by 0.4 seconds, that's awesome!

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.720
A trumpet!

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.440
The brass band practicing?

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.260
You can even hear it all the way out on the field.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.220
I wonder if that's Miyauchi-sempai?

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.890
Don't you realize that the rookie tournament is coming up?

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.200
It's not like all the first years get to participate.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.360
What is the team supposed to do with you?!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:55.410
But I just joined the track and field team because I liked running.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:59.290
I couldn't really see myself in competitions or being selected as the representative.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:04.760
Could it be that Hihara-sempai feels the same way about the school-wide competition?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:11.690
In the end I quit track and field and joined the brass band.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.970
But Yuu...

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:23.630
Yuu continued to work hard on his own, and eventually he was picked to participate in the tournament.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.310
So that's why I...

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:39.540
Kazuki!

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.670
Yuu, go for it!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:51.340
You'll be fine, I know it! Just do it like always!

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:54.090
Hey! That's dangerous, get down from there!

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.430
Yuu, you can do it!

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:02.360
What were you thinking, you idiot. That was so embarrassing.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:03.730
How'd you do?

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.020
Second.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.850
Wow! Awesome!

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:14.690
You know that your best time was better than I did today.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:17.450
If you had entered you could have won first place.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.080
First place?

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.250
Don't you think it's a waste you quit track and field?

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:29.200
No. 'Cause it's not like I've stopped running just because I quit track and field.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.000
I love to run!

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.930
But... I'm just no good at competitions.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:38.860
I try to concentrate, but I can feel the pressure coming down on me.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.510
I don't really hate it, but I'm just no good at it, I guess.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:46.580
But this here's different! I can just let it all out, like, bam!

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:48.560
It feels great!

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:53.350
I'm gonna get a lot better, and the next tournament I'll be sure to cheer you on!

00:09:56.390 --> 00:10:00.120
But Yuu ended up moving pretty soon after that.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.830
I haven't seen him for a long time.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.770
But getting second in a district tournament is really amazing.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.750
I'm sure that your trumpet helped give him the energy, Hihara-sempai.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:15.340
The sound of the trumpet resonates directly with the body.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:20.120
It vibrates the cells in the body and power flows into you.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:25.630
I also feel really energized whenever I hear you play, Hihara-sempai.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.880
Your trumpet gave me the power.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:35.140
You kind of sucked, but I could feel a ton of power rushing through my body!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.510
Thank you, Kazuki!

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:43.580
That student from General Studies is obviously going to get last place.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.730
It was impossible for her from the start.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.520
Kaho-chan, you're really trying hard, aren't you?

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:59.970
I've still got a long way to go. I've got to work harder.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:03.800
Kazuki Hihara will now perform!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:09.980
Hihara-sempai?

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:15.020
This might be all I can do for you.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.540
But if it cheers you up even a little bit...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.360
If my music can give you the energy...

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:42.560
I want to cheer up the people important to me! That's it! That's my music!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.970
Kaho-chan!

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.070
So he finally crossed that mountain...

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.820
Is that everything?

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:11.040
Yes. Thank you for your cooperation.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:08.740
How was it?

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:11.310
Not bad. You're getting better, little by little.

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:13.580
Mori-san, you don't have to hold back.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:16.440
I understand full well the level I am at.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.810
I want to hear your frank opinion.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.040
Hino-san...

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:28.050
Honestly, I think that it'll be hard for you to participate in the competition the way you are now.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.410
But I have hope.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:34.450
When I look at you practicing so intently, Hino-san,

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:39.460
I have a feeling like you'll show me something different than winning or what place you get, or something like that.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:45.440
The results of the final selection might be harsh,

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:48.180
but will you still be with me on stage?

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.930
Of course, OK!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.950
Thank you.

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.080
Her tone really needs work.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.790
Are you talking about Hino?

00:13:57.790 --> 00:13:58.810
Yeah.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.400
Well, I'm not going to mince words.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:06.320
I wonder if she'll hold out until the final selection.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.320
Maybe it's because she thrives on adversity...

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:14.660
I wonder...

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:19.940
Tsukimori, do you know anything about what's going on with Hino?

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.310
No, I don't know anything.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:29.340
Is she like Cinderella after the magic spell wore off?

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:34.240
Well, the shop keeper from Southern Music said something.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:38.340
He said that her hard work until now had been the real thing.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.010
That it wasn't magic.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.110
Kaho!

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.120
Kaho-chan!

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.350
Working hard?

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:52.080
Practicing is important, buy you have to make sure to eat properly!

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:55.780
You surprised me!

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:56.530
Here.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.270
Thank you, Mio. Thank you, Nao.

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:32.300
Kaho-sempai's sound...

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:36.750
Kaho-sempai has been practicing non-stop.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:43.340
I can feel Sempai's feeling of facing her music head on.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.710
They say that sweet things are good for when you are tired,

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:49.920
so I wonder if I should bake her some cookies?

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.470
It's like the sound is falling from the heavens.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.080
Amo-san!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:26.220
Ah, sorry! Am I bothering you?

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:31.920
But you see, Hino-san, you just seemed like the perfect subject to take a picture of there.

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.590
Oh, this brings back memories!

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:41.310
What's this?

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.080
When did you...

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.770
I call it: "The Dreaming Violinist!"

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.700
You don't have to title it.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:49.550
I'm confiscating this!

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:52.360
But I really liked that one.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.120
Do you have any others like this?

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.100
Nope, nope...

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:56.110
For real?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.120
Well, if you're talking about the ones I'm proud of...

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.710
You really looked like you were enjoying that performance.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:10.680
Even for someone that didn't know you, Hino-san, they'd think "That girl loves playing the violin."

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.530
I'm sure that message would come through.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:14.760
Here, you can have these.

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:16.010
It's OK?

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:20.140
Sure. They're all pictures of you while you're performing well.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:27.120
It's like, when a baseball player is in a slump, and they watch videos of when they were doing better, right?

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:28.520
Just like that.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.980
Amo-san...

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.320
Thank you.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.300
I have high expectations for your final selection!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:37.550
Hino-chan!

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:38.530
Huh?

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:41.340
See ya.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:47.830
Yunoki!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:48.970
Going home?

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:49.460
Yes.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.950
I see. You probably have a lot of things to get ready.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.380
Practicing again today?

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:58.370
Yeah! I'm really in a mood to practice right now.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:17:59.380
I see.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.560
Music really is great, don't you think?

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:04.600
See you.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:06.710
Yunoki.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:11.110
Congratulations on winning the third selection.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:15.330
Once I thought about it, I realized I'd never congratulated you properly.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:17.570
Thank you, Hihara.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:20.440
Good luck over there.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.460
Sure.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.100
Kanazawa-sensei...

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.730
It's way past the end of school already, you know.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.610
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:58.360
You're really trying hard every day, aren't you?

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:03.330
Well, even if I work like this now it might be too late to mean anything.

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:05.290
Hino.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:10.390
Uh, sometimes I get in a slump like this...

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:14.990
I've just decided to practice so much I don't have time to think about anything else.

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:17.300
You're really something, you know that?

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:21.560
I wasn't able to get over it.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.900
Be careful on your way home, all right?

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:41.120
I'll come to school early tomorrow and get some practice in.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.450
You're late today, aren't you?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:57.680
W-Wait a second, Yunoki-sempai!

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.430
No way...

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:12.640
Why do I feel like this has happened to me before?

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:19.650
What's the matter? Is it not to your taste?

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:22.150
No, it's delicious.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:26.090
Actually, it's the first time I've ever been to a fancy restaurant like this.

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:30.820
Since it's my final dinner, I figured it should be a bit luxurious.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.120
Final?

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:36.940
Will you continue playing the violin?

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.240
I'm not sure about the way I was before...

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:44.760
But all I'm thinking now is about doing my best and appearing in the final selection.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.430
You've still got that amazing will power.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.390
It's because you expect it of me, Yunoki-sempai.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:57.190
Sempai, you'll continue playing the flute in England, won't you?

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:03.660
Why is it that you have to go?

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:06.690
Are you saying that you want to be near my side?

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:08.830
N-No!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.020
It's just...

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:14.700
I just want you to continue playing music, Sempai.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:16.580
I don't want you to quit.

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:23.090
It was a lot of fun, Kahoko.

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:30.670
You were the best way to kill time.

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:39.730
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:46.430
The great 19th century German composer, pianist, and organist Mendelssohn

00:23:46.430 --> 00:23:51.400
left us mainly works for orchestra, piano and religious music.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:53.920
However his violin concerto is extremely famous.

00:23:53.920 --> 00:23:57.930
In Japan it's known lovingly as simply "Mencon."

00:23:57.930 --> 00:23:59.450
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:05.040
What was the name of the German literary master who Mendelssohn was deeply inspired by?

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:07.210
It's a secret showdown!

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:10.450
It's little Tsuchiura-kun versus little Tsukimori-kun!

00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:11.520
Why are we doing this?

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:13.580
That video, again?

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:15.470
I wonder if there are videos of anyone else?

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:18.090
Next episode: Our Cadenza.

00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:20.060
There isn't one for me.

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:23.950
The answer is... Goethe!
